<title>JAPAN: Sumitomo Trust problem loans (Banking account).</title>
<headline>Sumitomo Trust problem loans (Banking account).</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sumitomo Trust &amp; Banking Co Ltd has disclosed its restructured loans (in billions of yen unless specified):</p>
<p>					end-Sep 96     end-Mar 96</p>
<p>  Restructured loans	    150.6	    668.5</p>
<p>  Bad loans			 538.9	     27.1</p>
<p>  Non-performing loans	  392.1	    373.6</p>
<p>  Loans to troubled clients   235.3	    256.6</p>
<p>  Total problem loans	    1.32 trln	1.33 trln</p>
<p>Restructured loans are those on which interest rates have been cut to help corporate restructuring. Bad loans are to bankrupt firms and non-performing are those with interest payments in arrears by six months or more. Loans to troubled clients are mainly to the bank's non-bank affiliates.</p>
</text>
